WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.280
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.750
Hey, Playmaker...

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.220
You're Soulburner?

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.960
My name is Takeru Homura.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.140
What are you after?

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.600
Don't get the wrong idea.  I'm your ally.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.430
I'll show you proof.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:21.900
Ignis!

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.550
Kusanagi's brother's kidnappers and those 
who attacked Cyberse World are the same?

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.870
High probability.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.610
Then our priority is to 
find the escaped duelist.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.400
Where did they go?

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.980
Let's ask Kusanagi.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.820
He should be analyzing that duelist.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.830
This is...

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.840
It's Ghost Girl!

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.930
It's info about the restricted area.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.160
And how to enter the area.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.160
She want us to go to that area?

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.590
Don't!  It's a trap!

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.040
She's trying to trick us again!

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.170
But we have no other lead.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.640
Only that he vanished in that area.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.610
Even if it's a trap, we need 
to investigate that gate.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.980
Start stealth program.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.290
It seems Ghost Girl really does 
want us to go to the gate.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.190
Not necessarily.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.530
Playmaker!  Found you!

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.740
I told you so.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.900
Let's go!  We'll shake them off!

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.950
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:00.760
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:08.070
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.640
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:21.380
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:28.620
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:35.330
I want to share your pain

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.440
That's Go Onizuka.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.050
He got a job with SOL Technologies?

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.080
Go Onizuka's team has found Playmaker.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.780
He's...

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.400
From before...

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.160
Playmaker!

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.500
I'm happy you came back to LINK VRAINS!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.960
Humph!  But I'm disappointed!

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.300
Kenmochi!  Yoroizaka!

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.440
Surround him from both sides!  
Don't let him escape!

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.780
Roger!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.530
Let's battle, Playmaker!

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.410
We'll settle things today!

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.500
Playmaker, shall we duel him?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.080
No time for that.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.640
Let's shake them off!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.890
There ya go.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.620
I won't let you escape!

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.460
Hey!  That was dangerous!

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.330
Stay with them!  Go!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.530
Set a trap!

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.710
Don't let Playmaker escape!

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.570
They won't give up.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.630
They're as determined as us.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.920
Be careful!  It's a trap!

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.580
What should we do, Playmaker?

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.410
Keep going!

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.780
What?  Are you serious?

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.100
Manager Zaizen, we have 
info on the other duelist!

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.840
The account name is Soulburner!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.680
Soulburner...

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.510
When the Knights of Hanoi were defeated, 
this duelist with an Ignis showed up.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.090
And the battle between 
those who have Ignis...

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.660
What are they trying to do?

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.860
Is something about to happen 
in LINK VRAINS again?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.720
Remove the trap!

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.910
But keep observing them!

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.530
Roger!

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.910
That was easy!

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.300
But you didn't do anything.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.980
It's too early to feel safe.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:39.950
Since the traps are gone, it's 
easier for them to chase us.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.000
Onizuka is fired up!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.380
Playmaker, will you let me handle this?

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.390
What?

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:54.400
Playmaker vs Go Onizuka is a 
very appealing match for me.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.140
But I don't want you two to fight each other.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:04.350
Because you're both heroes 
that fought for LINK VRAINS.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.850
Okay.  I leave this to you.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.080
Good luck!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.250
Yeah!  You too!

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.980
I wasn't talking to you.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.320
So annoying!

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.000
Go Onizuka!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.130
I'm Soulburner!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.630
Who are you?  Don't interfere!

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.630
Please calm down, senpai!

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:32.790
Will you please duel me before Playmaker?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.090
Stop joking!

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.340
I have no time to play with you!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.160
But I have one too.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.280
Nice to meet you.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.280
What?  Then you're also...

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.850
Wait, Mr. Onizuka.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.090
What do you still want?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:56.560
Sorry.  I forgot to ask you 
the most important question.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.030
Well?  What?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:09.610
Why did you apply to be a 
bounty hunter for our company?

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:14.230
And throwing away your reputation 
as a charisma duelist.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.350
Why?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.510
Oh, that.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.950
It's so I could be myself!

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.390
Until I defeat him, I 
can't get back my pride!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.260
You mean Playmaker.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.730
That's right!

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:38.860
I heard SOL Technologies were after him, 
so I applied to be a bounty hunter!

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.000
I see.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:46.680
Then I'll tell you the secret 
to Playmaker's power.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:48.400
Secret?

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.890
I see.  You're also a victim 
of the Lost Incident.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:58.260
Exactly, Go Onizuka senpai!

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:02.860
Since you know, feel like dueling me now?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.680
You have no right to call me senpai!

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:11.870
But a bounty hunter's duty is 
to capture those who have Ignis.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.340
Fine.  I'll take you on.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.770
All right!

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:19.050
Once again, I'm Soulburner!

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.200
I'm the fire Ignis.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.820
I'm called Flame in this world.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.550
I never show mercy.  You 
may regret your decision!

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.290
Bring it on!

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.230
Speed Duel!

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.700
I'll go first!  My turn!

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.880
Flame, what do you think Go Onizuka will do?

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.710
Hmm, well...

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.200
He calls himself Go Onizuka.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.410
So he'll "go go" and attack.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.880
What do you think?

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.890
Hated that, huh?

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.880
I'll be serious then.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:03.720
According to Go Onizuka's battle history, 
his dueling continually evolves.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.430
So it's hard to estimate at this point.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.400
Don't let your guard down.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.130
I activate my Skill!  Dinowrestle Revolution!

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:19.100
From my deck, I activate the Field 
Spell, World Dino Wrestling!

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:25.210
When my Dinowrestler attacks 
your monster, it gains 200 ATK!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.120
What?  He already activated a Skill?

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:31.180
Didn't expect that.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:37.260
I summon Dinowrestler 
Capoeiraptor from my hand!

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.240
Dinowrestler?

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.210
He's not using his Gouki Deck anymore.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.150
So he's evolved a lot.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.120
It's impossible to predict this duel.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.210
He already surpassed our expectations.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.210
Go Onizuka is impressive!

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:02.330
From my hand, I activate the 
Continuous Spell, Dinomuscle!

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:07.080
The Dinowrestler on my field gains 400 ATK.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.190
I end my turn.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.870
Soulburner, show me your strength!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.130
I won't hold back!

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.810
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:25.310
I discard Salamangreat Falco to 
activate Salamangreat Meer's effect!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.870
It Special Summons itself from my hand!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:36.190
Then I return Salamangreat Meer to my hand 
to activate Salamangreat Falco's effect!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.290
It Special Summons itself from my graveyard!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:49.360
When Salamangreat Meer is added to my hand 
other than by a draw, I can Special Summon it!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:56.680
Then I summon Salamangreat 
Jack Jaguar from my hand!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.670
Three monsters!  He's going to...

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.650
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:12.250
The summoning conditions are at 
least two Fire Effect Monsters!

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.990
I set Salamangreat Falco, Meer and 
Jack Jaguar in the Link Markers!

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.130
Circuit combine!

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.160
Link Summon!

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:30.700
Appear, Link 3 Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.140
I see.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.540
That's your ace monster!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:56.050
Due to the Field Spell, 
World Dino Wrestling...

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.660
...Capoeiraptor's ATK become 2400 next turn.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.670
We must destroy it this turn.

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.410
That's right.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.270
Heatleo's effect!

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.270
When it's Link Summoned...

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:14.090
... I can return one card in your 
Spell and Trap Zone to your deck!

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.620
I return Dinomuscle!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.220
Dinomuscle's effect ends.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.190
Capoeiraptor's ATK return to normal.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.640
All right!  Here I go!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:35.140
When Heatleo is Link Summoned, Jack Jaguar's 
effect activates from the graveyard!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:40.510
I return a different Salamangreat 
in my graveyard to my deck.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:45.360
And I Special Summon this 
card next to Heatleo's link!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.480
I return Salamangreat Falco to my deck...

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:52.740
...and Special Summon Jack Jaguar next 
to Heatleo's link from my graveyard!

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.790
I set one card!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.760
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:03.230
Heatleo attacks Capoeiraptor!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.000
Heat Soul!

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:11.500
When Capoeiraptor is in attack position, 
it can't be destroyed in battle.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.400
What?

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.470
What!

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.850
But you still take damage!

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.180
And Capoeiraptor switches 
to defense position.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.680
I see.  That's an interesting card.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.150
I'll make sure to remember it.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:30.450
But we still have Jack Jaguar.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.290
Jack Jaguar can deal piercing damage 
to a monster in defense position!

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.670
Go, Salamangreat Jack Jaguar!

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.750
Too bad!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.170
The Field Spell, World 
Dino Wrestling's effect.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:49.910
When a Dinowrestler is on the field at the 
start of battle, only one monster can battle!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.150
What?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.760
That means you can't attack.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.770
Incredible!  You truly are incredible!

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.850
What are you trying to say?

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:09.690
Your dueling skills are impressive, but I'm 
really happy that I'm able to duel you!

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.660
I end my turn!

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:21.610
Go Onizuka!  As the hero who saved LINK 
VRAINS, can you provide a comment?

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:24.940
How's it feel to be an overnight sensation?

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:31.680
Well...  I'm satisfied just 
to see children smiling again.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:36.650
Can I ask you about the 
other hero - Playmaker?

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:40.970
After that incident, Playmaker vanished.

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:42.970
Do you know why?

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.460
No, I don't.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.670
Where do you think Playmaker is right now?

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:52.000
Have an idea of Playmaker's location?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:55.480
What's Playmaker's true identity?

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.010
Do you know?  Tell me!

00:14:58.010 --> 00:14:59.990
Give a comment about Playmaker!

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:03.760
If you duel him again, are you 
confident that you'll win?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.990
Go Onizuka, what's Playmaker's identity-

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.200
Be quiet!

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:11.700
They didn't care about me.

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.740
They only wanted to ask about Playmaker.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:21.730
I see.  But you three are the 
heroes who saved LINK VRAINS.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:25.800
You'll continue to be the focus of the press.

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:34.160
But we don't intend to acknowledge that the 
network was on the brink of destruction.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.780
So I ask you don't cause the 
press to delve into this.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:46.080
Playmaker always stands in my way.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.890
In dueling, even in life.

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:54.580
Until I defeat him, I can't 
take one step forward.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:16:02.310
That's why I threw away my name, status 
and honor as a charisma duelist.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:05.960
And became a bounty hunter 
for SOL Technologies.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.760
I don't care about the glory of the past.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:16.430
My only desire is to defeat Playmaker 
and gain the title as the true #1!

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:19.240
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.730
My defense position Capoeiraptor's 
effect activates.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:27.030
I Special Summon another 
Capoeiraptor from my deck!

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:34.620
Next, I summon Dinowrestler 
Capaptera from my hand!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.380
Appear!  My circuit!

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:46.540
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Dinowrestlers.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:52.430
I set two Dinowrestler Capoeiraptors 
and Capaptera in the Link Markers!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.430
Link Summon!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:17:02.100
Appear, Link 3 Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.870
Capaptera's effect now activates!

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.400
On the turn Capaptera is 
used to Link Summon...

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:15.810
...King T Wrextle gains 1000 
ATK until the end of battle!

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.290
4000 ATK...

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:21.050
This is pretty bad.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:27.060
Soulburner...  This person who has an Ignis 
is also a victim of the Lost Incident.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:32.500
That's the secret of Playmaker's power?

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:38.770
Yes.  The Lost Incident 
derailed Playmaker's life.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:45.240
For Playmaker, a duel 
means the same as living.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.650
Winning duels verifies his sense of self.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:52.220
And losing means losing yourself.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:56.570
His determination and persistence to win...

00:17:56.570 --> 00:18:02.000
I believe this is the secret 
to Playmaker's power.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:07.940
I don't know what the Lost 
Incident victims had to endure.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:13.800
But I didn't start dueling halfheartedly.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:19.810
I grew up not knowing my parents' faces.

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:24.160
In a world of survival of the fittest, 
I could only rely on myself.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.880
I was later put in an orphanage.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:31.190
That's where I encountered dueling.

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:35.050
I was instantly hooked on dueling.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:39.860
Until that moment, nothing ever satisfied me.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.330
But something about dueling did.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:46.300
Since then, dueling and 
I were always together.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:52.940
And before I knew it, I was 
famous as a charisma duelist.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:59.220
But I'm now here to be myself.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.510
To prove that I'm the strongest!

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:07.020
For the thirst for victory 
that's deep in my heart!

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:13.900
Go Onizuka is betting his life to dueling, 
so I won't take a single step back from you!

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.130
Battle!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:19.570
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle attacks Heatleo!

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:23.800
Then the Field Spell, World 
Dino Wrestling's effect!

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:30.250
King T Wrextle's ATK increase by 200 
during its attack on your monster!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.490
Then I'll use my set card to-

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:34.400
No you won't!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:39.120
Due to King T Wrextle's effect, 
you can't use spell or trap cards!

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.190
What?

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.530
Take this!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.730
Jurassic Howl!

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.330
Yeah!

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.040
How's that?

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.730
This is Go Onizuka's power!

00:19:55.730 --> 00:20:00.510
For everyone to appreciate me, I must win!

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:05.850
Playmaker is in my way and blocks my path!

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:08.360
Lost Incident victim, he says?

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:13.460
I know he suffered, but I 
also bet my life on dueling!

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:16.150
I'm the one who'll be #1!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:20.610
I'm not Playmaker's stepping stone!

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:25.010
I don't think you're a stepping stone.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:29.070
But right now, you're SOL 
Technologies's pet dog.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:34.300
Actually, a pitiful loser dog 
who complains to strangers.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:37.120
How dare you say that-

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.320
Go Onizuka!

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:44.230
The Go Onizuka in my 
heart is a great duelist.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:47.760
#1?  Everyone appreciate you?

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:52.500
The Go Onizuka I know won't 
say pathetic things like that!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:55.500
Be quiet!  What do you know!

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.480
I do know!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:21:01.710
Because Go Onizuka is a 
hero who gave me courage!

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:10.890
I admire you for defeating 
the ones who made us suffer.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:14.840
You gave me a path when 
I couldn't move forward.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.350
No matter how cornered he was...

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:23.360
...Go Onizuka was an independent duelist who 
believed in his own strength to the end!

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:29.100
Where's that person who gave me courage?

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:33.570
I end my turn.

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:39.590
By ending your turn, Dinowrestler King 
T Wrextle's ATK return to normal.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:45.340
Go Onizuka...  I want to duel the real you.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:50.170
And I'll fight the real you and win!

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:54.580
Because I have a reason why I can't lose too!

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.050
My turn!  I draw!

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:25.480
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:32.190
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:35.690
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:38.830
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:43.430
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:46.400
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:57.280
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.420
With repeating "nows"

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:04.350
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:10.330
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:13.600
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:41.080
By focusing on dueling, you can shake off 
your uncertainties and your sad past.

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:44.840
Onizuka and Soulburner 
have yet to achieve that.

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:49.700
They must break through their 
shells using their own power.

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:53.580
Dueling has the power to save them.

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:58.180
Go Onizuka is impressive.  
Regular moves won't work on him.

00:23:58.180 --> 00:24:01.660
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Hero In Name Only

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:04.080
Into the VRAINS!
